35,2,1,talk,Mio,,#### Turn 1 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The lab is down to one person with two hundred pieces waiting. The volunteers are mostly tied up with history walks. We are severely understaffed.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The data is clear. Head counts rise where mechanisms run, and visitors return because someone is present. Static displays fail.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The bay is capped at four hundred kilos per square metre. Last season, stonework required shoring and a rerouted delivery. The structure is already strained.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Two of our last four openings slipped because paperwork arrived after the shipping cut-off. We must plan for these delays, not just hope for the best.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, that staffing gap is terrifying! My loan costs ate a third of the budget, and mount-making rates jumped. We need self-supporting pieces to save money.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, self-supporting pieces are essential. With one conservator and a backlog, we cannot risk damage from complex mounts. We must choose simplicity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, your structural limits confirm my data. Mechanisms draw crowds, but if the bay cannot bear the weight, we must find a different way to keep the room alive.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, mechanisms are a liability. Seventeen call-outs last season, four during opening hours. The bay was roped off. We cannot risk that downtime again.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka, the shoring and yard reroute confirm my fears. Heavy items are a delivery nightmare. We must avoid anything that strains the bay or requires complex logistics.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Shion, I hear you! But if the bay can’t hold the weight, how do we keep the energy up without breaking the budget or the floor?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, simplicity is the only path. We lack the hands to maintain complex rigs. We must select an exhibition that stands on its own, requiring minimal intervention.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mio, the answer is presence, not weight. We need people working, not heavy machinery. The data proves static objects fail, but we can’t break the floor.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, presence is not a solution if the floor fails. I reject any proposal that risks the structure. We need stability, not spectacle.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I agree. Presence is vital, but we must ensure the delivery is safe. Let us avoid heavy items that strain the bay.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Shion, I love that idea! Lightweight, self-supporting pieces with live demonstrations would save our budget and keep the floor safe. Let’s hope the candidates match!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I concur. We need a proposal that respects our staffing limits and structural constraints. Let us see what options remain viable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Mio, precisely. Presence without structural risk. The candidates must prove they can deliver that balance. I am ready to evaluate them.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, I agree. Lightweight, self-supporting pieces with live demonstrations would save our budget and keep the floor safe. Let’s hope the candidates match!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, I am glad we are aligned. A safe, manageable delivery is the only way to avoid another season of apologies at the door.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
